; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Square Spiral
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     spiral, repeat, repcount, square
; SUMMARY:  Walks a little further after every right-angle turn, making a square spiral with a color for each direction.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The turtle walks, turns 90 degrees, and walks again, but every
;   side is a bit longer than the one before. Instead of closing into
;   a square, the path winds outwards into a square spiral. Every
;   side going up is red, right is yellow, down is green and left is
;   blue, so you can see the four directions.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change GROW in the last line to space the spiral out.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * REPCOUNT counts 1, 2, 3 ... as REPEAT goes round
;   * using REPCOUNT to make each side longer than the last
;   * REMAINDER to cycle through four colors
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change 90 to 120. What shape is the spiral now? Try 60 too.
;   * Count down instead: sides that get SHORTER, from the outside in.
;   * Make every side 3 longer instead of the same as its number.
; ============================================================

; Four colors, one for each direction the turtle can face.
make "colors [[220 50 50] [240 190 30] [50 160 80] [40 100 220]]

to squarespiral :sides :grow
  repeat :sides [
    setpencolor item 1 + remainder repcount - 1 4 :colors
    forward :grow * repcount
    right 90
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 248 240]
setpensize 4
squarespiral 66 8
